### Summary of the 5 Required Changes to the Pass-1 Brief

1. **Detector `extra` flags (`PR`, `NODN`) and `DRn` seeding/register split (`Q1(e)`, `Q3(f)`, `Q3(g)`, Section 7):**
   - Pass `PR` (`1 << 19`) in `extra` on all 8 `fcnvsd` rows (`FCNVSD` is architecturally defined only for `FPSCR.PR = 1` and reserved at `PR = 0`).
   - Add `NODN` to `fcnvsd fpul -0` to kill weakening `(f)` (`if (!(cpu->cd.sh.fpscr & SH_FPSCR_DN_ZERO)) ...`) at zero additional session cost.
   - Seed both destination halves (`frN` and `fr(N+1)`) with `0xdeadbeef` on `fcnvsd dr hi` / `fcnvsd dr lo`, and split destination registers between `DR0` (`0xf0ad` on `fcnvsd fpul 0.1` + `dr hi` / `dr lo`) and `DR2` (`0xf2ad` on the remaining 5 `fcnvsd fpul *` rows) so both weakening `(g)` (`ic->arg[0] != (size_t)&cpu->cd.sh.fr[0]`) and its mirror (`ic->arg[0] == (size_t)&cpu->cd.sh.fr[0]`) are killed at zero extra sessions.
   - *Shipped record status (`READ` / `MEASURED`):* **Already implemented** in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L228-L246) (Pass-2 dispositions F2, F3, F4, F5 in [brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p2.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p2.md#L21-L52)) and verified in [KILLTABLE.log](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/KILLTABLE.log#L14-L39).
2. **SH-4 NaN quiet-bit polarity (`Q1`, `Q2`, `Q4`, Sections 5–7):**
   - Under SH-4's architectural NaN encoding (`abs < 0x7fc00000` is `qNaN`; `abs >= 0x7fc00000` is `sNaN`), `0x7fc00000` is a **signaling NaN (`sNaN`)**, not a quiet NaN. Rename `fcnvsd fpul nan` $\to$ `fcnvsd fpul snan`, fix the existing `ftrcS-nan qNaN+` comment in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L176-L180), and file the [`ieee_store_float_value_rm`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L511-L515) `FP_NAN` quiet-bit polarity defect (`0x7fffffffffffffffULL` is an SH-4 `sNaN`, whereas SH-4 `qnan()` writes `0x7ff7ffffffffffff`).
   - *Shipped record status (`READ`):* **Already implemented** in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L176-L245) (dispositions F6, F9) and filed as `nanencoding` in [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L26104-L26106).
3. **Ledger and boundary premise corrections (`Q1(c)`, `Q1(d)`, Sections 2 & 6):**
   - Amend [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L8241) on two counts: (i) `#297` **guarded** the `(int32_t) op1.f` cast in [`X(ftrc_frm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2996-L3038) behind raw-bit range/NaN ladders rather than removing it, and (ii) `FCNVSD` does not destroy `FPUL` on *every* input because `+0.0` (`0x00000000`) is a fixed point (and `SR.FD = 1` faults first). Also correct Section 6's statement that `-2^31` (`0xcf000000`) is out-of-range C UB: `-2147483648.0` is exactly `INT32_MIN`, so `(int32_t)op1.f` is **well-defined** in C99 6.3.1.4p1 and produces `0x80000000` (which still corrupts `FPUL` from `0xcf000000` to `0x80000000`).
