#### Q1(a) — Does removing `cpu->cd.sh.fpul = (int32_t) op1.f;` leave the `DRn` output byte-identical for every `FPUL` value? (`READ` / `REASONED` / `MEASURED`)
- **For all `FPUL` inputs where `(int32_t) op1.f` has defined behaviour in C (`READ` / `REASONED`):** **Yes, unconditionally.** In [`X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3049-L3067):
  1. `ieee_interpret_float_value(cpu->cd.sh.fpul, &op1, IEEE_FMT_S);` at `:3056` reads `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` by value (`uint64_t x`) and populates local `struct ieee_float_value op1`.
  2. The subsequent lines (`uint64_t ieee = ieee_store_float_value(op1.f, IEEE_FMT_D);` and the two `reg(ic->arg[0])` stores) expand to `sh_dn(cpu, ieee_store_float_value_rm((op1.f), IEEE_FMT_D, IEEE_RM_RN))` ([cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L179-L194)). Neither [`ieee_store_float_value_rm`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L459-L716) nor [`sh_dn`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L179-L190) reads `cpu->cd.sh.fpul`.
- **Nuance for out-of-range / non-finite `FPUL` inputs (`REASONED` / `MEASURED`):** On `HEAD`, when `op1.f` is `NaN`, `±Inf`, or a finite value outside `(-2147483649.0, 2147483648.0)`, evaluating `(int32_t) op1.f` is **undefined behaviour** under C99 6.3.1.4p1. Under the abstract C machine, UB on `HEAD` means even the subsequent `DRn` store has no portable guarantee; on the x86_64 build host, `cvttsd2si` non-trappingly emits `0x80000000` into `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` without disturbing `op1.f`, so `DRn` is byte-identical across all $2^{32}$ inputs on x86_64 (`MEASURED` on `0.1`, `-0`, `inf`, `snan` in [witness_head.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out) vs [witness_fixed.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_fixed.out)).

#### Q1(b) — Does anything else in the tree rely on `FCNVSD` having changed `FPUL`? (`READ`)
- **No (`READ`).** Auditing every reference to `fpul` across `C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src`:
  - [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c): [`X(float_fpul_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2919-L2935) (`:2921`), [`X(ftrc_frm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2943-L3040) (`:2999, :3004, :3011, :3016, :3022, :3027, :3033, :3038`), [`X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3049-L3067) (`:3056`), [`X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3068-L3080) (`:3079`), [`X(fsca_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3094-L3103) (`:3096`), `STS FPUL,Rn` (`:4226`), `STS.L FPUL,@-Rn` (`:4597`), `LDS.L @Rm+,FPUL` (`:4602`), `LDS Rm,FPUL` (`:4607`), `FSTS FPUL,FRn` (`:5024`), `FLDS FRn,FPUL` (`:5030`).
  - [cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c): [`sh_cpu_new`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L141) (`CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32("fpul", cpu->cd.sh.fpul)`), [`sh_cpu_register_dump`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L768), and disassembly strings (`:1243, :1451, :1453, :1455`).
  - No dyntrans combiner, internal shadow state, or device reads `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` as a post-`FCNVSD` scratch value.
