    1. `#297` **guarded** the `(int32_t) op1.f` cast in `FTRC` behind raw-bit range/NaN ladders rather than removing it.
    2. `FCNVSD` on `HEAD` does not destroy `FPUL` on *every* input: `FPUL = 0x00000000` (`+0.0`) is a fixed point where `FPUL` remains `0x00000000` (and when `SR.FD = 1`, `FLOATING_POINT_AVAILABLE_CHECK` faults at `:3052` before reaching `:3057`).
  - *(Shipped record note: Caught in Pass-2 disposition F1 in [brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p2.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w576/brief_shfcnvsdfpul_p2.md#L15-L19) and Astra Change 4 in [codex_shfcnvsdp2late.txt](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/pass2_20261102/codex/codex_shfcnvsdp2late.txt#L288-L291).)*

#### Q1(d) — Is `+0` (`0x00000000`) the only in-range unchanged input? (`REASONED`)
- **Yes (`REASONED` by exhaustive domain proof across all $2^{32}$ bit patterns).**
- First, **a boundary correction to Section 6 of the Pass-1 brief (`READ` / `REASONED`):** Section 6 groups `-2^31` (`0xcf000000`, `op1.f = -2147483648.0`) with `+2^31` (`0x4f000000`, `op1.f = +2147483648.0`) under *"Finite single out of `int32_t` range (`|v| >= 2^31`): `(int32_t) op1.f` is C UB"*. In two's-complement `int32_t`, `INT32_MIN` is $-2^{31} = -2147483648$, so by C99 6.3.1.4p1, `(int32_t)(-2147483648.0)` is **well-defined** and yields `INT32_MIN` (`(uint32_t)0x80000000`). Because `0x80000000 != 0xcf000000`, `FPUL` is still corrupted on `0xcf000000`, just by a defined cast rather than UB. (The shipped comment in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L218) already separates `0xcf000000` `-2^31 -> 0x80000000` from the UB class.)
- Now let $u \in [0, 2^{32}-1]$ be the initial `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` bit pattern, $S = u \gg 31 \in \{0, 1\}$, $E = (u \gg 23) \mathbin{\&} \text{0xff} \in [0, 255]$, $m = u \mathbin{\&} \text{0x7fffff} \in [0, 2^{23}-1]$, and $v = \text{op1.f}$ as decoded by [`ieee_interpret_float_value`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L196-L315). For `HEAD` to leave `FPUL` unchanged on an in-range input ($-2^{31} \le v < 2^{31}$), we need:
  $$u = \text{cast}(v) \triangleq \text{(uint32\_t)(int32\_t)}v.$$
  1. **Zero, subnormal, and $|v| < 1.0$ ($E \in [0, 126]$, i.e. `0x00000000`..`0x3f7fffff` and `0x80000000`..`0xbf7fffff`):**
     Here $|v| < 1.0$, so `(int32_t)v == 0` and $\text{cast}(v) = \text{0x00000000}$. Thus $u = \text{cast}(v)$ holds **if and only if $u = \text{0x00000000}$ (`+0.0`)**. (In particular, `-0.0` has $u = \text{0x80000000} \ne \text{0x00000000}$.)
  2. **Positive normal $1.0 \le v < 2^{31}$ ($S = 0$, $E \in [127, 157]$, unbiased exponent $e = E - 127 \in [0, 30]$, `0x3f800000`..`0x4effffff`):**
     Here $u = E \cdot 2^{23} + m \ge 127 \cdot 2^{23} = 1{,}065{,}353{,}216$ (`0x3f800000`), while $\text{cast}(v) = \lfloor (1 + m \cdot 2^{-23}) 2^e \rfloor < 2^{e+1}$.
     - If $e \le 29$ ($E \le 156$), $\text{cast}(v) < 2^{30} = 1{,}073{,}741{,}824$. The only exponent in $[127, 156]$ with $E \cdot 2^{23} < 2^{30}$ is $E = 127$ ($e = 0$), where $\text{cast}(v) = 1 \ne u \ge 1{,}065{,}353{,}216$.
     - If $e = 30$ ($E = 157$), $\text{cast}(v) = 2^{30} + 128m$ is exact (since $e = 30 > 23$). Setting $u = \text{cast}(v)$:
       $$157 \cdot 2^{23} + m = 2^{30} + 128m \implies 127m = (157 - 128) \cdot 2^{23} = 29 \cdot 2^{23} = 243{,}269{,}632.$$
       Because $243{,}269{,}632 = 127 \times 1{,}915{,}508 + 116 \not\equiv 0 \pmod{127}$ (indeed $\gcd(127, 29 \cdot 2^{23}) = 1$ since $127$ is a Mersenne prime), there is **no integer solution** $m$.
  3. **Negative normal $-2^{31} \le v \le -1.0$ ($S = 1$, $E \in [127, 158]$, $e = E - 127 \in [0, 31]$, `0xbf800000`..`0xcf000000`):**
     Here $u = 2^{31} + E \cdot 2^{23} + m$, and in two's complement $\text{cast}(v) = 2^{32} - \lfloor |v| \rfloor$. Setting $u = \text{cast}(v)$ requires:
     $$E \cdot 2^{23} + m = 2^{31} - \lfloor |v| \rfloor \implies \lfloor |v| \rfloor = (256 - E) \cdot 2^{23} - m.$$
     Since $E \le 158$ and $m < 2^{23}$, the right-hand side is $> (256 - 159) \cdot 2^{23} = 97 \cdot 2^{23} > 2^{29}$, which forces $e \in \{29, 30, 31\}$ ($E \in \{156, 157, 158\}$):
     - $e = 31$ ($E = 158, m = 0$, $v = -2^{31}$): $u = \text{0xcf000000} \ne \text{cast}(v) = \text{0x80000000}$.
     - $e = 30$ ($E = 157$): $\lfloor |v| \rfloor = 2^{30} + 128m = 128 \cdot 2^{23} + 128m$, while $(256 - 157) \cdot 2^{23} - m = 99 \cdot 2^{23} - m < 128 \cdot 2^{23} \le \lfloor |v| \rfloor$, impossible.
     - $e = 29$ ($E = 156$): $\lfloor |v| \rfloor = 2^{29} + 64m = 64 \cdot 2^{23} + 64m$. Setting $64 \cdot 2^{23} + 64m = 100 \cdot 2^{23} - m$ gives $65m = 36 \cdot 2^{23} = 301{,}989{,}888$. Since $\gcd(65, 2^{23}) = 1$ and $65 \nmid 36$ ($301{,}989{,}888 = 65 \times 4{,}645{,}998 + 18$), there is **no integer solution** $m$.
  - **(Bonus check on the UB range on x86_64):** On x86_64 where `cvttsd2si` returns `0x80000000` for every out-of-range/Inf/NaN input, every such input has $E \ge 158$, whereas `0x80000000` has $E = 0$. Therefore, across all $2^{32}$ possible `FPUL` values on x86_64, **`0x00000000` (`+0.0`) is the unique fixed point**.

#### Q1(e) — Cold-debugger seeds (`fpul`, `fpscr`, `r1`, `frn`) and `sts fpul,r2` + `mov.l r2,@r1` under `step 3` (`READ` / `MEASURED`)
- **Debugger register seeds (`READ`):** In [`sh_cpu_new`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L140-L190), `"fpscr"`, `"fpul"`, `"r0"`..`"r15"`, `"fr0"`..`"fr15"`, and `"xf0"`..`"xf15"` are registered via `CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32`, binding directly to `cpu->cd.sh.fpscr`, `cpu->cd.sh.fpul`, `cpu->cd.sh.r[i]`, `cpu->cd.sh.fr[i]`, and `cpu->cd.sh.xf[i]`. When the debugger executes an assignment (`fpul = ...`, `fpscr = ...`, etc.), [`debugger_assignment`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1796-L1854) calls [`debugger_parse_name`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_expr.c#L93-L174) with `writeflag = DEBUGGER_EXPR_WRITE`, which writes directly to the underlying `uint32_t` field via `settings_access`. (Writing `fpscr` directly via settings does not call `sh_update_fpscr`, which only swaps `fr[]`/`xf[]` when `FPSCR.FR` toggles; because `FR = 0` throughout `sh_rounding_probe.py`, direct writes to `fpscr` take immediate effect on `SH_FPSCR_PR`, `SH_FPSCR_DN_ZERO`, and `SH_FPSCR_RM`.)
- **4-instruction / `step 3` visibility (`READ` / `MEASURED`):** In [`run_batch`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L298-L322), when `word2` is non-zero, `put w 0x8c010000, word` writes `(sts_fpul_r2 << 16) | insn` (`fcnvsd` at `0x8c010000`, `sts fpul,r2` `0x025a` at `0x8c010002` in little-endian memory) and `put w 0x8c010004, word2` writes `(0x0009 << 16) | 0x2122` (`mov.l r2,@r1` at `0x8c010004`, `nop` at `0x8c010006`). In [`debugger_cmd_step`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1717-L1741), `step 3` sets `debugger_n_steps_left_before_interaction = 2` (`n - 1`), so the single-step loop in [`debugger`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger.c#L822-L832) executes exactly 3 instructions (`fcnvsd`, `sts fpul,r2` via [`X(copy_fp_register)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4224-L4228), and `mov.l r2,@r1`) before re-entering the prompt and running `dump 0x8c010100`.
- **Live confirmation (`MEASURED`):** Confirmed in [witness_head.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out) (`3/6`), [witness_fixed.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_fixed.out) (`6/6`), [base_head.raw](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/base_head.raw) (`40/52`), and [fixed.raw](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/killtable_20261102/fixed.raw) (`52/52`).

