### Q2 — The Partition of the $2^{32}$ `FPUL` Input Space (`READ` / `REASONED`)

Assuming `SR.FD = 0` (when `SR.FD = 1`, both `HEAD` and the fixed handler take `FLOATING_POINT_AVAILABLE_CHECK` at [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3052) before touching `FPUL` or `DRn`), the $2^{32}$ possible 32-bit `FPUL` values partition into **1 unchanged class** and **9 changed classes**:

| # | Class | `FPUL` 32-bit hex range(s) | `HEAD` post-`FCNVSD` `FPUL` | Fixed post-`FCNVSD` `FPUL` | Section 7 detector row(s) / disclosure status |
| :- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1** | **Positive zero (`+0.0`)** *(unchanged)* | `0x00000000` (1 value) | `0x00000000` (unchanged fixed point) | `0x00000000` (unchanged) | **No row** (cannot discriminate `HEAD` vs fix; disclosed in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L219-L220)). |
| **2** | **Negative zero (`-0.0`)** *(changed)* | `0x80000000` (1 value) | `0x00000000` (sign bit cleared) | `0x80000000` | **`fcnvsd fpul -0`** (`0x80000000`). |
| **3** | **Positive normal in $[1.0, 2^{31})$** *(changed)* | `0x3f800000`..`0x4effffff` | `0x00000001`..`0x7fffff80` (`(int32_t)op1.f`, never equal to `FPUL` per Q1(d)) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **`fcnvsd fpul 1.5`** (`0x3fc00000` $\to$ `HEAD` `0x00000001`). |
| **4** | **Negative normal in $(-2^{31}, -1.0]$** *(changed)* | `0xbf800000`..`0xceffffff` | `0xffffffff`..`0x80000080` (`(uint32_t)(int32_t)op1.f`, never equal to `FPUL` per Q1(d)) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **`fcnvsd fpul -1.5`** (`0xbfc00000` $\to$ `HEAD` `0xffffffff`). |
| **5** | **Exact $-2^{31}$ (`-2147483648.0`)** *(changed, defined C cast)* | `0xcf000000` (1 value) | `0x80000000` (`INT32_MIN`, defined in C99 6.3.1.4p1) | `0xcf000000` | **No row** (disclosed in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L218)). |
| **6** | **Nonzero normal in $(-1.0, 1.0)$** *(changed)* | `0x00800000`..`0x3f7fffff` (`+`), `0x80800000`..`0xbf7fffff` (`-`) | `0x00000000` (truncated toward zero) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **`fcnvsd fpul 0.1`** (`0x3dcccccd`), plus **`fcnvsd dr hi`** and **`fcnvsd dr lo`** on `DR0`; negative fraction in $(-1.0, 0)$ not separately rowed. |
| **7** | **Subnormals ($\pm 2^{-149}$..$\pm(1-2^{-23})2^{-126}$)** *(changed)* | `0x00000001`..`0x007fffff` (`+`), `0x80000001`..`0x807fffff` (`-`) | `0x00000000` ([`ieee_interpret_float_value`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L261-L265) decodes to nonzero $|v| < 2^{-126} < 1$, cast yields `0`) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **No row** (deliberately omitted to avoid coupling to `#303`'s `DN=1` input-flush gap; disclosed in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L218-L219)). |
| **8** | **Finite out-of-`int32_t`-range ($v \ge 2^{31}$ or $v < -2^{31}$)** *(changed, C UB)* | `0x4f000000`..`0x7f7fffff` (`+`), `0xcf000001`..`0xff7fffff` (`-`) | C UB (`0x80000000` via `cvttsd2si` on x86_64) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **No row** (disclosed in [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L216-L218); UB path itself is exercised by `inf` and `snan`). |
| **9** | **Infinities (`+Inf`, `-Inf`)** *(changed, C UB)* | `0x7f800000` (`+Inf`), `0xff800000` (`-Inf`) | C UB (`0x80000000` on x86_64) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **`fcnvsd fpul inf`** (`0x7f800000`); `-Inf` (`0xff800000`) is disclosed. |
| **10** | **NaNs (`qNaN` and `sNaN`)** *(changed, C UB)* | SH-4 `qNaN`: `0x7f800001`..`0x7fbfffff`, `0xff800001`..`0xffbfffff`; SH-4 `sNaN`: `0x7fc00000`..`0x7fffffff`, `0xffc00000`..`0xffffffff` | C UB (`0x80000000` on x86_64) | Preserved (`FPUL`) | **`fcnvsd fpul snan`** (`0x7fc00000`, named `fcnvsd fpul nan` in Pass-1 brief); SH-4 `qNaN` is disclosed ([sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L216-L217)). |

