### Q4 — Option-Set Completeness, Sibling Audit, and Neighbouring Questions (`READ`)

#### 1. Is `DELETE` the only architectural option for `X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`? (`READ`)
- **Yes (`READ`).** Per the SH-4 programming manual (`sh4_programming.txt:10866-10909, :16935`, inlined in Section 5 of the brief), `FCNVSD FPUL,DRn` only reads `FPUL` and writes `DRn` (plus `FPSCR` exception flags on `DENORM`/`sNaN`). There is no architectural write to `FPUL` to replace the line with; deleting `cpu->cd.sh.fpul = (int32_t) op1.f;` is the entire fix for `X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`.

#### 2. Audit of Sibling FP/Communication-Register Handlers in `src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c` (`READ`)
Every handler touching `cd.sh.fpul` or converting between formats in [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c) was inspected (`READ`):
- [`X(float_fpul_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2919-L2935) (`FLOAT FPUL,FRn` / `FLOAT FPUL,DRn`): reads `int32_t fpul = cpu->cd.sh.fpul;`, writes `FRn` or `DRn`; **does not write `fpul`**.
- [`X(ftrc_frm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2943-L3040) (`FTRC FRm,FPUL` / `FTRC DRm,FPUL`): reads `FRm` or `DRm`, writes `cpu->cd.sh.fpul` via the `#297` raw-bit range/NaN ladder; **architecturally writes `FPUL`**.
- [`X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3049-L3067) (`FCNVSD FPUL,DRn`): the subject of `#576`.
- [`X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3068-L3080) (`FCNVDS DRm,FPUL`): reads `DRm` (`fr[r8]` / `fr[r8+1]`), converts to single via [`ieee_store_float_value_rm(op1.f, IEEE_FMT_S, sh_fp_rm(cpu))`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3079), and writes `cpu->cd.sh.fpul`; **architecturally writes `FPUL` and does not overwrite `DRm`**.
- [`X(fsca_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3094-L3103) (`FSCA FPUL,DRn`): reads `cpu->cd.sh.fpul`, writes `sin`/`cos` to `fr[r8+0]` and `fr[r8+1]`; **does not write `fpul`**.
- `STS FPUL,Rn` ([`:4224-4228`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4224-L4228)), `STS.L FPUL,@-Rn` ([`:4595-4599`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4595-L4599)), `FSTS FPUL,FRn` ([`:5021-5025`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L5021-L5025)): read `fpul` only.
- `LDS.L @Rm+,FPUL` ([`:4600-4604`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4600-L4604)), `LDS Rm,FPUL` ([`:4605-4609`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4605-L4609)), `FLDS FRn,FPUL` ([`:5028-5031`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L5028-L5031)): write `fpul` only.
- **Result (`READ`):** No other handler in [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c) has a spurious write to `cd.sh.fpul` (or to its source register).

#### 3. Disposition of the Three Neighbouring Items in Section 8 (`READ`)
1. **`PR = 0` on `FCNVSD` / `FCNVDS` (`READ`):**
   - In [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c), `#316` added `FPSCR.PR` checks only to [`X(fsrra_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3283-L3299) (`PR = 1` reserved) and the odd-register `PR = 1` cases of [`X(fneg_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3202-L3219) and [`X(fabs_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3230-L3244). Neither the `PR = 1`-only instructions ([`X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3049-L3067), [`X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3068-L3080)) nor the remaining `PR = 0`-only instructions ([`X(fsca_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3094-L3103), [`X(fipr_fvm_fvn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3115-L3132), [`X(ftrv_xmtrx_fvn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3144-L3179), [`X(fldi_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3191-L3196), [`X(fmac_fr0_frm_frn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3537-L3550)) nor the global `[SZ, PR] = 11` check are implemented.
   - **Verdict:** **FILE as a separate class (`shfpprreserved`)** rather than expanding `#576` beyond its one-site contract. As noted in Change 4 above, ensure `shfpprreserved` (already named at [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L226)) is actually filed in [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md).
2. **`FCNVDS` has no detector row in `sh_rounding_probe.py` (`READ` / `MEASURED`):**
   - **Verdict:** Keep `fcnvds ctl` (`DR2 = 1.5 -> FPUL = 0x3fc00000`) in the rung-3 witness ([sh_fcnvsd_witness.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/sh_fcnvsd_witness.py#L136), where it is already `MEASURED` passing in both [witness_head.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_head.out#L8) and [witness_fixed.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shfcnvsdfpul/witness_20261102/witness_fixed.out#L8)), and **do not** add an `FCNVDS` row to `sh_rounding_probe.py` in this round (`X(fcnvds_drm_fpul)` is untouched by `#576`).
3. **`DN = 1` subnormal input on `FCNVSD` (`READ`):**
   - **Verdict:** **Leave alone here and disclose.** [`ieee_interpret_float_value`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L217-L225) explicitly documents `#303`'s contract (*"SH-4's FPSCR.DN ... stays NOT modelled ... operands decode per DN=0-with-completion while subnormal RESULTS still flush"*), tracked under `qhshfpexcept` ([OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L24083)).

#### 4. Something Else Found While Verifying (`READ`)
- **SH-4 NaN quiet-bit polarity (`F6` / `F9` / `nanencoding`, Change 2):** Section 5's manual excerpt (`:10948`) shows `if (abs < 0x7fc00000) return(qNaN); else return(sNaN);`. On SH-4, quiet NaNs have fraction MSB = 0 and signaling NaNs have fraction MSB = 1, so `0x7fc00000` is an **SH-4 `sNaN`**, not a `qNaN`, and [`ieee_store_float_value_rm`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/float_emul.c#L511-L515) (`r |= 0x7fffffffffffffffULL`) emits an SH-4 `sNaN` (`0x7fffffffffffffff`) instead of SH-4's canonical `qNaN` (`0x7ff7ffffffffffff`). *(Already adopted in Pass 2: row renamed `fcnvsd fpul snan`, `ftrcS-nan` relabeled `sNaN+` at [sh_rounding_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_rounding_probe.py#L176-L245), and `nanencoding` filed at [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L26104-L26106).)*
- **Product comment precision (Change 4):** The working-tree comment in [`X(fcnvsd_fpul_drn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L3057-L3061) states *"FCNVSD reads FPUL and writes DRn only (SH-4 Programming Manual §9.29)"*. Because §9.29 also updates `FPSCR` on `DENORM` or `sNaN` (`set_I()` / `set_E()`), qualifying that clause (e.g. *"writes DRn only (FPSCR exception flags unmodelled per qhshfpexcept); it never modifies FPUL"*) avoids overstating §9.29.

